meta {
  name: Concat - Mixed URL Response
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/concat/mixed?response_mode=url
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  response_mode: url
}

body:multipart-form {
  request_json: {
    "segments": [
      {"type": "silence", "source": "(500ms)"},
      {"type": "server_file", "source": "concatenation_test/01-sarah-audio.mp3"},
      {"type": "upload", "index": 0},
      {"type": "server_file", "source": "concatenation_test/02-mark-audio.mp3"},
      {"type": "upload", "index": 1},
      {"type": "silence", "source": "(1s)"},
      {"type": "server_file", "source": "concatenation_test/03-sarah-audio.mp3"}
    ],
    "export_formats": ["wav", "mp3"],
    "normalize_levels": true,
    "crossfade_ms": 200,
    "trim": true,
    "trim_threshold_ms": 150,
    "output_filename": "professional_mix",
    "project": "podcast/episode01"
  }
  uploaded_files: @file(./test-files/audio-sample-1.wav)
  uploaded_files: @file(./test-files/audio-sample-2.wav)
}

docs {
  # Audio Concatenation - Mixed URL Response
  
  Complete mixed-mode workflow with JSON response containing detailed metadata and file information.
  
  ## Input Method
  - **Content-Type**: multipart/form-data
  - **Multiple Uploads**: Two files in this example (index 0 and 1)
  - **Complex Segment Ordering**: 7 segments with mixed types
  
  ## Response Mode
  - **response_mode=url**: Returns JSON with URLs and metadata
  - Detailed processing information included
  - File paths and durations provided
  
  ## Response Structure
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Audio concatenation completed successfully",
    "output_files": [
      "podcast/episode01/professional_mix.wav",
      "podcast/episode01/professional_mix.mp3"
    ],
    "total_duration_seconds": 78.5,
    "file_count": 5,
    "processing_time_seconds": 3.2,
    "metadata": {
      "type": "concat",
      "timestamp": "2025-10-29T14:30:22.456Z",
      "generation_info": {
        "audio_segment_count": 5,
        "silence_segment_count": 2,
        "upload_count": 2,
        "crossfade_applied": true,
        "normalization_applied": true,
        "trim_applied": true,
        "processing_details": [
          {
            "type": "silence",
            "duration_ms": 500,
            "source": "(500ms)"
          },
          {
            "type": "server_file",
            "filename": "01-sarah-audio.mp3",
            "duration_seconds": 15.0,
            "trim_info": {
              "trimmed": true,
              "leading_silence_removed_ms": 150,
              "trailing_silence_removed_ms": 100
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "upload",
            "index": 0,
            "duration_seconds": 12.3
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Advanced Features
  This example demonstrates the complete feature set:
  - Multiple file uploads (2 files)
  - Mixed segment types (server files + uploads + silence)
  - Audio trimming with custom threshold
  - Crossfade transitions
  - Audio normalization
  - Custom output filename
  - Project folder organization
  - Multiple export formats
  - Detailed metadata response
  
  ## Project Organization
  - **project**: "podcast/episode01"
  - **output_filename**: "professional_mix"
  - **Result**: Saved to outputs/podcast/episode01/professional_mix.{wav,mp3}
  
  ## Use Cases
  - Professional podcast production workflows
  - Complex audio assembly with user content
  - Web applications requiring detailed feedback
  - Batch processing with comprehensive logging
  - Quality control and validation workflows
  
  ## Tips
  - URL mode provides complete processing details
  - Use for debugging and validation
  - Monitor trim_info to verify silence removal
  - Check processing_time for performance optimization
  - project parameter creates nested folder structure
}
